   1666  f4ac							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1667  f4ac							; DeriveEnemyY — live Y for enemy slot X. Moving types are DERIVED, not stored:
   1668  f4ac							; there is no free ZP byte for per-slot movement state (phase/direction live
   1669  f4ac							; in the shared EnemyRamP/EnemyRamD bitfields), so the formula is
   1670  f4ac							; re-evaluated from ROM spawn + the EnemyRamP frame clock at each refresh.
   1671  f4ac							; Bat:     spawn..spawn+2, 1 px / 2 frames, triangle(EnemyRamP>>1 & 3).
   1672  f4ac							; Tentacle: spawn..spawn+2, 1 px / 8 frames, triangle(EnemyRamP>>3 & 3).
   1673  f4ac							; Spider:  spawn..spawn+24, 1 px / 4 frames, p=(EnemyRamP>>2)&63,
   1674  f4ac							;	    down first with dwell at top: delta = p<25 ? p : (p<48 ? 48-p : 0).
   1675  f4ac							;	    Gate ÷4 (not spec ÷8): phase period must divide the 256-step clock
   1676  f4ac							;	    wrap — 48-step÷8 phases never align (teleport), 64-step÷4 does.
   1677  f4ac							;	    Dwell absorbs the 256 mod 64 leftover (wrap lands in dwell zone).
   1678  f4ac							; Clock:   EnemyRamP, inc'd once per frame in RefreshEnemyY (TickCounter is
   1679  f4ac							;	    the 60-frame game timer — gates from it wrap every second).
   1680  f4ac							; Other types: straight ROM y (their movement stages come later).
   1681  f4ac							; In: X = enemy slot. Out: A = live Y. Clobbers A/Y.
   1682  f4ac							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1683  f4ac				   DeriveEnemyY
   1684  f4ac							; --- Fold batch (P3.1): enemy records live in bank2; stage per entry so
   1685  f4ac							; any caller works. Stage is A/X-only — caller's slot in X survives. ---
